Authors and provenance
======================

This project is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 or
later; see COPYING for the full text. The licence descends from the Warsow
"hrace" race gametype, whose source headers carry the copyright notice below,
and applies to the whole of server/racemod/ as a derivative work.

The race gametype (server/racemod/)
-----------------------------------

Chasseur de bots
    Original author of the Warsow hrace race gametype.
    "Copyright (C) 2009-2010 Chasseur de bots", GPL-2.0-or-later — the notice
    carried by source/progs/gametypes/hrace.as and hrace/entities/items.as.
    (Upstream marks only those two files; this fork keeps that convention
    rather than adding headers the original project did not carry.)

hettoo
    Author of much of the practice/recall tooling this lineage is built on.
    hrace/positionstore.as is noted in-file as "ported verbatim from
    hettoo/wsw-race@racemod", and hrace.as carries several "hettoo:"-attributed
    behaviours (spawn handling, the practicemode message on spectators, and
    skipping warmup/countdown).

DenMSC ("msc")
    Maintainer of https://github.com/DenMSC/wsw-race, branch `racemod`, which
    is the exact upstream this fork was taken from at commit
    c63f9f394657f4e091fa5f6ca04da2ddfd9b404c (2021-09-16). Several behaviours
    in hrace.as remain attributed "msc:" in-line (permanent practicemode
    message, the MAX_ACCEL replacement, the overtime check).

racesow.org contributors
    Sean Reed and contributors, 2026 — the racesow.org layer: central stats
    reporting, the cross-server mesh, tournaments, achievements, the WR ghost,
    live map/MOTD/announcement polling, and the base-gametype fixes listed in
    the project's upstream-patch queue.

The surrounding server, site and infrastructure
-----------------------------------------------

Everything outside server/racemod/ (the web application, engine patches,
Docker images, deployment tooling) is by the racesow.org contributors, and is
distributed under the same licence.

Third-party components retain their own licences: Warsow and Warfork
themselves, the qfusion engine lineage the enginepatches apply to, and the
prejump/projectile natives vendored from Gelmo/warfork-racemod into
warfork/enginepatches/.
